@startuml
' Behavior 2: WAN outage -> Outbox buffering -> reconnect -> replay.
' Authored in Slice 2. Renders through scripts/render-diagrams.sh.
!include style.puml
title Components-and-Connectors view: behavior, outage, buffering, replay

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 230

participant "POS Adapter" as POSAD #dae8fc
participant "Store Agent" as SA #d5e8d4
database "Store-Local\nInventory" as SLI #e1d5e7
queue "Outbox" as OB #e1d5e7
participant "Communications\nFront-End" as CFE #fff2cc
participant "Subscribers" as SUB #fff2cc

== WAN link down ==
loop every sale during the outage
  POSAD -> SA : Inventory Event
  SA -> SLI : apply (reads and writes continue)
  SA -> OB : append
end
OB -x CFE : publish fails; events held
note over OB : buffers in order\n(~180,000 events per 30 min at 100/s)

== WAN link restored ==
OB -> CFE : replay-from-sequence (last acknowledged)
CFE --> OB : acknowledge each
CFE -> SUB : notify (gap filled)
note over SUB : duplicates ignored by event ID;\nresync closes any remaining gap

legend right
  Store-local reads and writes never stop during the
  outage. On reconnect the Outbox replays from the last
  acknowledged sequence number, so no event is lost.
endlegend
@enduml
